namespace Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay

/-- **Stacks 00R9.** Let `k` be a field and `S` a finite type `k`-algebra which is Cohen–Macaulay
(every local ring `S_𝔭` satisfies `depth_{𝔪}(S_𝔭) = dim S_𝔭`) and equidimensional of dimension
`d`. Let `f = f₁, …, f_i` be elements of `S` cutting out a nonempty closed subset
`V(f₁, …, f_i)` of `Spec S` of dimension at most `d - i`. Then that dimension is exactly `d - i`,
and `f₁, …, f_i` is a regular sequence in `S_𝔮` for every prime `𝔮 ⊇ (f₁, …, f_i)`. -/
@[stacks 00R9 "Cohen-Macaulayness of a Noetherian local ring is `Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay A A`
(Definition 00N8); that of the Noetherian ring `S` (Definition 00NC) is spelled out over its
localizations at primes, as in tag 00ND. `dim V(f₁, …, f_i)` is `ringKrullDim (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f)`
(`ringKrullDim_quotient`), and `≤ d - i` is written `+ f.length ≤ d` in `WithBot ℕ∞`, the source's
truncating subtraction being false as stated. The extra hypothesis `Ideal.ofList f ≠ ⊤` excludes
the empty locus, where the source's equality fails. See the module docstring."]
public theorem ringKrullDim_quotient_add_length_eq_and_isRegular
    {k S : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S] [Algebra.FiniteType k S]
    (hS : ∀ (p : Ideal S) [p.IsPrime],
      Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime p))
    (hequi : TopologicalSpace.Equidimensional (PrimeSpectrum S)) (d : ℕ)
    (hd : ringKrullDim S = d) (f : List S) (hf : Ideal.ofList f ≠ ⊤)
    (hdim : ringKrullDim (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f) + f.length ≤ (d : WithBot ℕ∞)) :
    ringKrullDim (S ⧸ Ideal.ofList f) + f.length = (d : WithBot ℕ∞) ∧
      ∀ (q : Ideal S) [q.IsPrime], Ideal.ofList f ≤ q →
        ∀ (Sq : Type*) [CommRing Sq] [Algebra S Sq] [IsLocalization.AtPrime Sq q],
          RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular Sq (f.map (algebraMap S Sq)) :=
    by exact Stacks.CohenMacaulay.EquidimensionalCut.solution (k := k) hS hequi d hd f hf hdim

end Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay

end

/-!
# A Cohen-Macaulay finite type algebra over a field is equidimensional in each dimension

Let `k` be a field and let `S` be a Cohen-Macaulay `k`-algebra of finite type. This file proves
Stacks 00OV: the local dimension of `X = Spec S` is a locally constant function with finitely many
values, and its level set `T_d` is equidimensional of dimension `d`.

Everything comes from one identity (`height_eq_coheight_of_isMin`): *for a minimal prime `q` of
`S` and a maximal ideal `𝔪 ⊇ q`, the height of `𝔪` is the coheight of `q`*, that is every
irreducible component of `X` through a point has the dimension of the local ring there. Both
descriptions of the local dimension given by Lemma 00OT enter its proof:

* `coheight q ≤ height 𝔪`, because `V(q)` is an irreducible component through `q`, so
  `coheight q = dim V(q) ≤ dim_q X = min {height 𝔪' | 𝔪' ⊇ q}`;
* `height 𝔪 ≤ coheight q`, because a Cohen-Macaulay local ring is equidimensional
  (`ringKrullDim_eq_coheight_of_isMin`): the dimension formula `dim R = dim R_p + dim R/p` in
  `R = S_𝔪` (Lemma 00NA) at the minimal prime `p = q S_𝔪`, whose height is `0`, gives
  `height 𝔪 = dim S_𝔪 = dim S_𝔪/q S_𝔪 = coheight (q S_𝔪) ≤ coheight q`.

So all the numbers `height 𝔪` for `𝔪` a maximal ideal above `x` and all the numbers `coheight q`
for `q` a minimal prime below `x` are one and the same, and `dim_x X`, being the infimum of the
former by Lemma 00OT, is that number (`localKrullDim_eq_coheight`).

Consequently the local dimension is constant along `≤`, so its level set `T_d` is stable under
both generalization and specialization, and it is open because the set of points `p` all of whose
minimal primes lie below a fixed `x` is open — `Spec S` has finitely many irreducible components.
Each `T_d` is then a union of the sets `V(q)` for the minimal primes `q` it contains, and these
are precisely its irreducible components: the generic point of a component of `T_d`, which exists
because an open subspace of `Spec S` is sober, lies above a minimal prime `q`, and maximality
forces the component to be `V(q)`, of dimension `coheight q = d`. The dimension of `T_d` itself is
`d` because it contains such a `V(q)` while every one of its points has coheight at most `d` in
it, and the range of the local dimension is finite because it is contained in the image of the
finite set of minimal primes under `coheight`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.CohenMacaulay.Equidimensional.solution`: the statement of Stacks 00OV.

## Implementation notes

*Lemma 00N9 is used through its sibling 00NA.* The source deduces "all components through a point
of `Spec S` have the dimension of the local ring there" from the fact that all maximal chains of
primes of `S_𝔪` have length `dim S_𝔪` (Lemma 00N9). Turning that into the inequality
`height 𝔪 ≤ coheight q` needs a maximal chain *starting at the given minimal prime* `q S_𝔪`, whose
existence is a separate well-foundedness argument; Lemma 00NA — the dimension formula in a
Cohen-Macaulay local ring, which the source proves from the same chain statement — gives the
inequality outright at `p = q S_𝔪`, in the form "a Cohen-Macaulay local ring is equidimensional".
Only Lemma 00OT is needed besides, and 00OS enters through it.

*Two facts used here are missing from Mathlib.* That the topological Krull dimension of a
quasi-sober subspace of `Spec R` is the order-theoretic Krull dimension of its poset of primes
(`topologicalKrullDim_eq_krullDim`; Mathlib has `PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocusEquivIrreducibleCloseds`
for a zero locus only); that a subspace of a subspace has the dimension of the corresponding
subspace of the ambient space (that one the library has, as
`topologicalKrullDim_preimage_val` in `StacksFrontier.Topology.Dimension.Krull`); and that the set
of points
whose minimal primes all lie below a fixed point is open (`isOpen_setOf_forall_isMin_le`).

## References

* [StacksProject 00OV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00OV)
-/



namespace Stacks.CohenMacaulay.Equidimensional

open Stacks.Spectrum.LocalDimension

open Order PrimeSpectrum TopologicalSpace

section Topology

end Topology

section Spectrum

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R]

/-- The set of primes containing a given prime is closed. -/
private lemma isClosed_Ici (q : PrimeSpectrum R) : IsClosed (Set.Ici q) :=
  zeroLocus_asIdeal q ▸ isClosed_zeroLocus _

/-- The closure of a point in a subspace of `Spec R` is the set of primes of the subspace above
it. -/
private lemma closure_singleton_subtype {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum R)} (w : ↥T) :
    (closure {w} : Set ↥T) = Subtype.val ⁻¹' Set.Ici (w : PrimeSpectrum R) := by
  ext v
  rw [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_Ici, le_iff_specializes, ← subtype_specializes_iff,
    specializes_iff_mem_closure]

/-- The dimension of the irreducible closed subset `V(q)` is the coheight of `q`. -/
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_Ici (q : PrimeSpectrum R) :
    topologicalKrullDim (Set.Ici q) = (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have := (isClosed_Ici q).isClosedEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober
  rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_krullDim]
  exact (coheight_eq_krullDim_Ici q).symm

/-- `V(q)` is an irreducible component of `Spec R` for `q` a minimal prime. -/
private lemma Ici_mem_irreducibleComponents {q : PrimeSpectrum R} (hq : IsMin q) :
    Set.Ici q ∈ irreducibleComponents (PrimeSpectrum R) := by
  rw [← zeroLocus_asIdeal, zeroLocus_ideal_mem_irreducibleComponents, q.isPrime.radical]
  exact isMin_iff.mp hq

/-- Every point of `Spec R` has a minimal prime below it. -/
private lemma exists_isMin_le (x : PrimeSpectrum R) : ∃ q : PrimeSpectrum R, IsMin q ∧ q ≤ x := by
  obtain ⟨Q, hQ, hQle⟩ := Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_le (I := ⊥) (J := x.asIdeal) bot_le
  exact ⟨⟨Q, hQ.1.1⟩, isMin_iff.mpr hQ, (asIdeal_le_asIdeal _ _).mp hQle⟩

/-- The set of minimal primes of a Noetherian ring is finite. -/
private lemma finite_setOf_isMin [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    {q : PrimeSpectrum R | IsMin q}.Finite :=
  Set.Finite.subset (Set.Finite.preimage (f := PrimeSpectrum.asIdeal)
    (fun _ _ _ _ h => PrimeSpectrum.ext h) (minimalPrimes.finite_of_isNoetherianRing R))
    fun _ hq => isMin_iff.mp hq

end Spectrum

section CohenMacaulay

/-- **A Cohen-Macaulay local ring is equidimensional.** In a Noetherian local Cohen-Macaulay ring
every minimal prime has coheight the dimension of the ring: the dimension formula
`dim A = dim A_p + dim A/p` (Lemma 00NA) at a prime `p` of height `0`. -/
@[sga "2 III 3.9" "special case"]
private lemma ringKrullDim_eq_coheight_of_isMin {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A]
    [IsLocalRing A] (hA : Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay A A) {p : PrimeSpectrum A}
    (hp : IsMin p) : ringKrullDim A = (coheight p : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : p.asIdeal.IsPrime := p.isPrime
  have hheight : p.asIdeal.height = 0 := (height_eq_orderHeight p).trans (height_eq_zero.mpr hp)
  rw [hA.ringKrullDim_eq_height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient p.asIdeal, ringKrullDim_quotient,
    zeroLocus_asIdeal, ← coheight_eq_krullDim_Ici, hheight]
  simp

/-- **The Cohen-Macaulay input.** In a Noetherian ring all of whose local rings are
Cohen-Macaulay, the height of a maximal ideal `m` is at most the coheight of any minimal prime `q`
below it: `height m = dim S_m` is the coheight of the minimal prime `q S_m` of `S_m`, and
coheights only grow along the strictly monotone `Spec S_m → Spec S`. -/
private lemma height_le_coheight_of_isMin {S : Type*} [CommRing S] [IsNoetherianRing S]
    (hS : ∀ (p : Ideal S) [p.IsPrime],
      Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime p))
    {q m : PrimeSpectrum S} (hq : IsMin q) (hqm : q ≤ m) : height m ≤ coheight q := by
  have : m.asIdeal.IsPrime := m.isPrime
  have : IsLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) := Localization.AtPrime.isLocalRing _
  set e := IsLocalization.AtPrime.primeSpectrumOrderIso (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) m.asIdeal
  obtain ⟨p, hep⟩ : ∃ p, e p = ⟨q, hqm⟩ := ⟨e.symm _, e.apply_symm_apply _⟩
  -- `p` is a minimal prime of `S_m`, being the preimage of the minimal prime `q` of `S`
  have hqmin : IsMin (⟨q, hqm⟩ : ↥(Set.Iic m)) := fun b hb =>
    Subtype.coe_le_coe.mp (hq (Subtype.coe_le_coe.mpr hb))
  have hpmin : IsMin p := e.isMin_apply.mp (hep ▸ hqmin)
  have hcoh : coheight p ≤ coheight q := by
    have h := (coheight_le_coheight_apply_of_strictMono e e.strictMono p).trans
      (coheight_le_coheight_apply_of_strictMono Subtype.val (fun _ _ h => h) (e p))
    rwa [hep] at h
  have hdim : ((height m : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) = ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime m.asIdeal) := by
    rw [IsLocalization.AtPrime.ringKrullDim_eq_height m.asIdeal, ← height_eq_orderHeight]
  have := (hdim.trans (ringKrullDim_eq_coheight_of_isMin (hS m.asIdeal) hpmin)).trans_le
    (by exact_mod_cast hcoh : ((coheight p : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ (coheight q : ℕ∞))
  exact_mod_cast this

end CohenMacaulay

section FiniteType

variable (k : Type u) [Field k] {S : Type v} [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]
  [Algebra.FiniteType k S]
  (hS : ∀ (p : Ideal S) [p.IsPrime],
    Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime p))

include k in
/-- The dimension of an irreducible component of `Spec S` through a minimal prime `q` is at most
the height of any maximal ideal above `q`: both are compared to the local dimension at `q` through
Lemma 00OT. -/
private lemma coheight_le_height_of_isMin {q m : PrimeSpectrum S} (hq : IsMin q) (hm : IsMax m)
    (hqm : q ≤ m) : coheight q ≤ height m := by
  have h00OT := localKrullDim_eq_iSup_irreducibleComponents_and_eq_iInf_height k q
  have h₁ : (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) q := by
    rw [h00OT.1, ← topologicalKrullDim_Ici q]
    exact le_biSup (fun Z : Set (PrimeSpectrum S) => topologicalKrullDim Z)
      ⟨Ici_mem_irreducibleComponents hq, Set.mem_Ici.mpr le_rfl⟩
  have h₂ : localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) q ≤ (m.asIdeal.height : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
    rw [h00OT.2]
    exact iInf₂_le m.asIdeal ⟨isMax_iff.mp hm, (asIdeal_le_asIdeal _ _).mpr hqm⟩
  rw [← height_eq_orderHeight]
  exact_mod_cast h₁.trans h₂

include k hS in
/-- **All components through a point have the dimension of the local ring there.** For a minimal
prime `q` below a maximal ideal `𝔪` of a Cohen-Macaulay finite type `k`-algebra, the height of `𝔪`
is the coheight of `q`. -/
private lemma height_eq_coheight_of_isMin {q : PrimeSpectrum S} (hq : IsMin q) {𝔪 : Ideal S}
    (h𝔪 : 𝔪.IsMaximal) (hq𝔪 : q.asIdeal ≤ 𝔪) :
    (𝔪.height : WithBot ℕ∞) = (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have : 𝔪.IsPrime := h𝔪.isPrime
  have : IsNoetherianRing S := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k S
  have hqm : q ≤ (⟨𝔪, ‹𝔪.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum S) := (asIdeal_le_asIdeal _ _).mp hq𝔪
  rw [height_eq_orderHeight (⟨𝔪, ‹𝔪.IsPrime›⟩ : PrimeSpectrum S)]
  exact_mod_cast le_antisymm (height_le_coheight_of_isMin hS hq hqm)
    (coheight_le_height_of_isMin k hq (isMax_iff.mpr h𝔪) hqm)

include k hS in
/-- **The heart of Stacks 00OV.** The local dimension of `Spec S` at `x` is the coheight of any
minimal prime below `x`, that is the dimension of any irreducible component through `x`: by
Lemma 00OT it is the least height of a maximal ideal above `x`, and all of those heights are the
coheight of `q`. -/
private lemma localKrullDim_eq_coheight {q x : PrimeSpectrum S} (hq : IsMin q) (hqx : q ≤ x) :
    localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) x = (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
  have hqx' : q.asIdeal ≤ x.asIdeal := (asIdeal_le_asIdeal _ _).mpr hqx
  obtain ⟨𝔪₀, h𝔪₀, hx𝔪₀⟩ := Ideal.exists_le_maximal x.asIdeal x.isPrime.ne_top
  rw [(localKrullDim_eq_iSup_irreducibleComponents_and_eq_iInf_height k x).2]
  refine le_antisymm ((iInf₂_le 𝔪₀ ⟨h𝔪₀, hx𝔪₀⟩).trans_eq
    (height_eq_coheight_of_isMin k hS hq h𝔪₀ (hqx'.trans hx𝔪₀))) (le_iInf₂ fun 𝔪 h𝔪 => ?_)
  exact (height_eq_coheight_of_isMin k hS hq h𝔪.1 (hqx'.trans h𝔪.2)).ge

include k hS in
/-- The level sets of the local dimension are open: around a point `x` the set of points whose
minimal primes all lie below `x` is an open neighbourhood on which the local dimension is the
common coheight of those minimal primes. -/
private lemma isLocallyConstant_localKrullDim :
    IsLocallyConstant (localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S)) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing S := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k S
  rw [IsLocallyConstant.iff_isOpen_fiber]
  intro d
  rw [isOpen_iff_forall_mem_open]
  intro x hx
  refine ⟨{p : PrimeSpectrum S | ∀ q : PrimeSpectrum S, IsMin q → q ≤ p → q ≤ x}, fun p hp => ?_,
    isOpen_setOf_forall_isMin_le x, fun _ _ h => h⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqp⟩ := exists_isMin_le p
  rw [Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, localKrullDim_eq_coheight k hS hq hqp,
    ← localKrullDim_eq_coheight k hS hq (hp q hq hqp)]
  exact hx

include k hS in
/-- Every point of a level set `T` of the local dimension has a minimal prime `q` below it of
coheight `d`, and then the whole of `V(q)` lies in `T`, the local dimension being constant on
`V(q)`. -/
private lemma exists_isMin_of_mem_fiber {d : WithBot ℕ∞} {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)}
    (hTd : T = localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) {x : PrimeSpectrum S} (hx : x ∈ T) :
    ∃ q : PrimeSpectrum S, IsMin q ∧ q ≤ x ∧ (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) = d ∧ Set.Ici q ⊆ T := by
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqx⟩ := exists_isMin_le x
  rw [hTd, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff] at hx
  have hqd : (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞) = d := (localKrullDim_eq_coheight k hS hq hqx).symm.trans hx
  refine ⟨q, hq, hqx, hqd, fun p hp => ?_⟩
  rw [hTd, Set.mem_preimage, Set.mem_singleton_iff, localKrullDim_eq_coheight k hS hq hp, hqd]

/-- A level set of a locally constant function on `Spec S` is open, hence quasi-sober. -/
private lemma quasiSober_of_eq_fiber {d : WithBot ℕ∞} {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)}
    (h : IsLocallyConstant (localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S)))
    (hTd : T = localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) : QuasiSober ↥T :=
  (hTd ▸ h.isOpen_fiber d : IsOpen T).isOpenEmbedding_subtypeVal.quasiSober

include k hS in
/-- Every irreducible component of a level set `T` of the local dimension is the set `V(q)` of
primes above a minimal prime `q` lying in `T`, hence has dimension `d`: the generic point of the
component, which exists because `T` is open in the sober space `Spec S`, lies above a minimal
prime `q`, and `V(q)` is an irreducible subset of `T` containing the component. -/
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber {d : WithBot ℕ∞} {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)}
    (hTd : T = localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) {Z : Set ↥T}
    (hZ : Z ∈ irreducibleComponents ↥T) : topologicalKrullDim Z = d := by
  have := quasiSober_of_eq_fiber (isLocallyConstant_localKrullDim k hS) hTd
  obtain ⟨z, hzZ⟩ : ∃ z : ↥T, Z = closure {z} :=
    ⟨hZ.1.genericPoint,
      (hZ.1.closure_genericPoint (isClosed_of_mem_irreducibleComponents Z hZ)).symm⟩
  obtain ⟨q, hq, hqz, hqd, hqT⟩ := exists_isMin_of_mem_fiber k hS hTd z.2
  -- `V(q)` is irreducible in `T` and contains `Z`, so it is `Z`
  have hWirr : IsIrreducible (Subtype.val ⁻¹' Set.Ici q : Set ↥T) := by
    rw [← closure_singleton_subtype (⟨q, hqT (Set.mem_Ici.mpr le_rfl)⟩ : ↥T)]
    exact isIrreducible_singleton.closure
  have hZW : Z ⊆ (Subtype.val ⁻¹' Set.Ici q : Set ↥T) := by
    rw [hzZ, closure_singleton_subtype z]
    exact Set.preimage_mono (Set.Ici_subset_Ici.mpr hqz)
  rw [hZW.antisymm (hZ.2 hWirr hZW), topologicalKrullDim_preimage_val _ _ hqT,
    topologicalKrullDim_Ici]
  exact hqd

include k hS in
/-- A nonempty level set `T` of the local dimension has dimension `d`: it contains the set `V(q)`
of dimension `coheight q = d` for a minimal prime `q` below any of its points, and every point of
`T` has coheight at most `d` in `T`, having such a minimal prime below it too. -/
private lemma topologicalKrullDim_fiber {d : WithBot ℕ∞} {T : Set (PrimeSpectrum S)}
    (hTd : T = localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) (hT : T.Nonempty) :
    topologicalKrullDim ↥T = d := by
  have := quasiSober_of_eq_fiber (isLocallyConstant_localKrullDim k hS) hTd
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hT
  obtain ⟨q, -, -, hqd, hqT⟩ := exists_isMin_of_mem_fiber k hS hTd hx
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [topologicalKrullDim_eq_krullDim, krullDim_eq_iSup_coheight]
    refine iSup_le fun w => ?_
    obtain ⟨q', -, hq'w, hq'd, -⟩ := exists_isMin_of_mem_fiber k hS hTd w.2
    calc ((coheight w : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ((coheight q' : ℕ∞) : WithBot ℕ∞) := by
          exact_mod_cast (coheight_le_coheight_apply_of_strictMono Subtype.val
            (fun _ _ h => h) w).trans (coheight_anti hq'w)
      _ = d := hq'd
  · rw [← hqd, ← topologicalKrullDim_Ici q, ← topologicalKrullDim_preimage_val _ _ hqT]
    exact topologicalKrullDim_subspace_le ↥T _

end FiniteType

public theorem solution {k S : Type*} [Field k] [CommRing S] [Algebra k S]
    [Algebra.FiniteType k S]
    (hS : ∀ (p : Ideal S) [p.IsPrime],
      Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay (Localization.AtPrime p) (Localization.AtPrime p)) :
    IsLocallyConstant (localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S)) ∧
      (∀ d : WithBot ℕ∞,
        Equidimensional ↥(localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) ∧
          ((localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}).Nonempty →
            topologicalKrullDim ↥(localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S) ⁻¹' {d}) = d)) ∧
        (Set.range (localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S))).Finite := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing S := Algebra.FiniteType.isNoetherianRing k S
  refine ⟨isLocallyConstant_localKrullDim k hS, fun d => ⟨fun Z hZ W hW => ?_,
    topologicalKrullDim_fiber k hS rfl⟩, ?_⟩
  · rw [topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber k hS rfl hZ,
      topologicalKrullDim_component_fiber k hS rfl hW]
  · refine Set.Finite.subset
      ((finite_setOf_isMin (R := S)).image fun q => (coheight q : WithBot ℕ∞)) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨q, hq, hqx⟩ := exists_isMin_le x
    exact ⟨q, hq, (localKrullDim_eq_coheight k hS hq hqx).symm⟩

end Stacks.CohenMacaulay.Equidimensional

/-!
# A Cohen-Macaulay finite type algebra over a field is equidimensional in each dimension

Let `k` be a field and let `S` be a Cohen-Macaulay `k`-algebra of finite type. Then `Spec S`
breaks up, as a finite disjoint union of open and closed subsets,
$$
  \operatorname{Spec}(S) = \coprod_d T_d,
$$
where `T_d` is equidimensional of dimension `d`: all of its irreducible components have
dimension `d`. Equivalently, `S` is a finite product of rings `S_d` all of whose maximal ideals
have height `d`.

The reason is that a Cohen-Macaulay local ring is equidimensional — all its maximal chains of
primes have length `dim` (Lemma 00N9) — so every irreducible component of `Spec S` through a
point `x` has dimension exactly the local dimension `dim_x Spec S` at `x`, and not merely at most
that (Lemma 00OS, Lemma 00OT). Since `Spec S` is Jacobson, two components that meet already meet
in a closed point (Lemmas 00G1, 00G3), so components that meet have equal dimension; as there are
only finitely many of them (Lemmas 00FO, 00FQ), grouping them by their common dimension gives the
decomposition.

## Main results

* `PrimeSpectrum.isLocallyConstant_localKrullDim_and_equidimensional_fiber_and_finite_range`:
  the local dimension of `Spec S` is a locally constant function with finitely many values, and
  each of its level sets is equidimensional of the corresponding dimension.

## Implementation notes

*The family `T_d` is pinned, as the fibers of the local dimension.* The source's `T_d` is not
just some clopen decomposition: `T_d` is the set of points at which the dimension is `d`, that is
the fiber of `TopologicalSpace.localKrullDim (PrimeSpectrum S)` over `d` (Topology Definition
0055 (4), already in this library). Taking the family to be those fibers rather than an
existentially quantified one is what makes this the source's statement instead of a weaker
existence claim, and it pays for itself: `Spec S = \coprod_d T_d` — disjointness and covering —
is then definitional, "`T_d` is open and closed" is `IsLocallyConstant.isClopen_fiber` applied to
the first conjunct, and "the union is finite" is finiteness of the range, the third conjunct.

*The index runs over `WithBot ℕ∞`, not over `0, …, dim S`.* That is where `localKrullDim` takes
its values, so the fibers cover `Spec S` with no side condition. The source's range is recovered
from the conclusion: `T_d` is empty unless `d` is a natural number at most `dim S`, since a
nonempty `T_d` has dimension `d` and sits inside `Spec S`. For the same reason the dimension of a
fiber is asserted only when the fiber is nonempty — `topologicalKrullDim ∅ = ⊥`, not `d`.

*The equivalent product decomposition is not restated.* "`S` is a product of rings `S_d` such
that every maximal ideal of `S_d` has height `d`" is the image of the clopen decomposition under
Lemma 00EM, which matches decompositions of `Spec S` into open and closed pieces with
decompositions of `S` into products; the source itself derives the second form from the first
that way. Restating it would add an existential over rings and no mathematics. Its condition on
maximal ideals is also already available: for a maximal ideal `𝔪` the local dimension at `𝔪` is
`𝔪.height`, because `𝔪` is the only maximal ideal above itself, so by Lemma 00OT the maximal
ideals lying in `T_d` are exactly those of height `d`.

*Cohen-Macaulayness of `S`.* Definition 00NC asks that all local rings of the Noetherian ring `S`
be Cohen-Macaulay, and Cohen-Macaulayness of a Noetherian local ring is
`Module.IsMaximalCohenMacaulay A A` (Definition 00N8), so the hypothesis is spelled out over the
localizations of `S` at its primes, as in tags 00ND and 00R9. `IsNoetherianRing S` is not assumed
separately: it follows from `Algebra.FiniteType k S`.

Faithfulness to [StacksProject 00OV].

1. No hypothesis is dead. `Field k` cannot be weakened to a commutative ring: `S = ℤ_p` is a
   regular, hence Cohen-Macaulay, finite type `ℤ_p`-algebra whose spectrum has the generic point
   at local dimension `0` and the closed point at local dimension `1`, and the fiber over `0` is
   the non-closed `{(0)}`, so the first conjunct fails. `Algebra.FiniteType k S` cannot be
   dropped: the same computation in the non-finite-type `k`-algebra `k[t]_{(t)}` gives the same
   failure. Cohen-Macaulayness cannot be dropped: for `S = k[x, y, z] ⧸ (xy, xz)`, the plane
   `x = 0` meeting the line `y = z = 0`, the local dimension is `1` along the line away from the
   origin and `2` on the plane, and the fiber over `2` is the plane, which is closed but not
   open, so again the first conjunct fails.
2. The base and the ring are the source's: `k` is a field, `S` is a `k`-algebra of finite type,
   and the topology, the dimensions and the Cohen-Macaulay condition are all those of `S` itself
   — no base change and no polynomial ring presenting `S`.
3. The decomposition the source names is pinned, not asserted to exist: `T_d` *is* the level set
   of the local dimension, and the conclusion is an equation determining its dimension together
   with the local constancy that makes it open and closed, not the existence of some family with
   those properties.
4. The instantiation is not degenerate: for `S = k[x, y] × k[z]` the local dimension takes the
   two values `2` and `1`, `T_2` is the plane and `T_1` the line, both nonempty, clopen and
   equidimensional of their dimensions, so the decomposition genuinely has more than one piece;
   for `S = k[x, y]` there is one piece, of dimension `2`; `S = k` is the degenerate instance.

